From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwsim: rearm operstate after frame registration refresh

The hwsim AP restart paths release stale management and EAPOL receive sockets
before start_bss(), but wifi_drv_set_operstate() treats vap_configured as a
guard.  Because the flag remains true, its state=1 callback returns early and
does not create replacement sockets.  The AP therefore continues beaconing
without delivering authentication frames to embedded hostapd.

Mark the hwsim VAP unconfigured whenever those receive registrations are
released.  The normal start_bss() callback can then rebuild exactly one fresh
registration set and restore the configured flag.  Cover both the individual
VAP restart and the radio-wide wiphy reconfiguration paths.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 wifi_hal_nl80211.c       | 5 +++++
 wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
index 6fe5149..cf5d68b 100644
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -8361,6 +8361,11 @@ int nl80211_update_wiphy(wifi_radio_info_t *radio)
                     unregister_data_frame_socket(interface);
                 }
 #endif /* EAPOL_OVER_NL */
+                /* Let start_bss() rebuild the receive paths through the
+                 * normal set_operstate(1) callback.  Otherwise its configured
+                 * guard returns before registering replacement sockets. */
+                interface->vap_configured = false;
+
 #endif /* HWSIM_RADIO */
 
                 nl80211_enable_ap(interface, false);
diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c
index 65f5e44..7c3aa0a 100644
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c
@@ -6352,6 +6352,11 @@ int restart_interface(wifi_interface_info_t *interface)
             unregister_data_frame_socket(interface);
         }
 #endif /* EAPOL_OVER_NL */
+        /* Let start_bss() rebuild the receive paths through the normal
+         * set_operstate(1) callback.  Otherwise its configured guard returns
+         * before registering replacement sockets. */
+        interface->vap_configured = false;
+
 #endif /* HWSIM_RADIO */
 
         if (nl80211_enable_ap(interface, false) < 0) {
